.TH NEMUE-FUZZ 1 "November 2025" "Nemue 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nemue-fuzz \- Web content discovery and fuzzing
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nemue fuzz
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.I URL

.SH DESCRIPTION
High-performance web content discovery and fuzzing tool. Supports directory enumeration, file discovery, subdomain enumeration, parameter fuzzing, and cloud storage discovery.

.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I URL
Target URL or domain (e.g., https://example.com or example.com for DNS mode)

.SH OPTIONS
.SS Fuzzing Modes
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Fuzzing mode: dir, file, ext, vhost, subdomain, s3, azure, gcp. Default: dir
.IP
.B dir
- Directory enumeration
.IP
.B file
- File discovery
.IP
.B ext
- Extension fuzzing
.IP
.B vhost
- Virtual host discovery
.IP
.B subdomain
- DNS subdomain enumeration
.IP
.B s3
- AWS S3 bucket discovery
.IP
.B azure
- Azure Blob storage discovery
.IP
.B gcp
- Google Cloud Storage discovery

.SS Wordlists
.TP
.BR \-w ", " \-\-wordlist " " \fIFILE\fR
Custom wordlist file path
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-builtin " " \fINAME\fR
Built-in wordlist: dirs1k, dirs10k, files, extensions, subdomains, params, wordpress, joomla, laravel, api
.TP
.B \-\-mutate
Apply mutations to wordlist (l33t speak, case variations, year suffixes)

.SS Performance
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-concurrency " " \fINUM\fR
Concurrent requests (default: 50)
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-rate-limit " " \fINUM\fR
Rate limit in requests per second
.TP
.B \-\-timeout " " \fISECONDS\fR
Request timeout in seconds (default: 10)

.SS Filtering
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-status-codes " " \fICODES\fR
Filter by status codes (comma-separated, e.g., 200,301,302)
.TP
.B \-\-exclude-status " " \fICODES\fR
Exclude specific status codes
.TP
.B \-\-min-size " " \fISIZE\fR
Minimum response size in bytes
.TP
.B \-\-max-size " " \fISIZE\fR
Maximum response size in bytes
.TP
.B \-\-match-regex " " \fIPATTERN\fR
Match response body with regex pattern
.TP
.B \-\-exclude-regex " " \fIPATTERN\fR
Exclude responses matching regex
.TP
.B \-\-wildcard-detection
Enable wildcard response detection

.SS Recursive Discovery
.TP
.BR \-R ", " \-\-recursive
Enable recursive directory scanning
.TP
.B \-\-max-depth " " \fINUM\fR
Maximum recursion depth (default: 3)

.SS Extensions & Parameters
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-extensions " " \fIEXTS\fR
File extensions to append (comma-separated, e.g., php,asp,html)
.TP
.B \-\-param-mode " " \fIMODE\fR
Parameter fuzzing mode: sniper, clusterbomb, pitchfork, replace

.SS HTTP Options
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-headers " " \fIHEADERS\fR
Custom headers (key:value pairs, comma-separated)
.TP
.BR \-U ", " \-\-user-agent " " \fIUA\fR
Custom User-Agent string
.TP
.B \-\-follow-redirects
Follow HTTP redirects
.TP
.B \-\-max-redirects " " \fINUM\fR
Maximum redirect hops (default: 5)

.SS Output
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output-format " " \fIFORMAT\fR
Output format: text, json, csv, markdown, html. Default: text
.TP
.BR \-O ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Save results to file

.SH BUILT-IN WORDLISTS
.TP
.B dirs1k
1,000+ common directories
.TP
.B dirs10k
10,000+ extended directories
.TP
.B files
Common files (backups, configs, sensitive files)
.TP
.B extensions
40+ file extensions (.php, .asp, .jsp, .bak, etc.)
.TP
.B subdomains
Common subdomains (www, mail, api, dev, etc.)
.TP
.B params
GET/POST parameters (id, user, page, etc.)
.TP
.B wordpress
WordPress-specific paths
.TP
.B joomla
Joomla CMS paths
.TP
.B laravel
Laravel framework paths
.TP
.B api
REST/GraphQL API endpoints

.SH FUZZING MODES
.SS Directory Enumeration
Discover hidden directories on web servers. Uses FUZZ placeholder in URL path.

.SS File Discovery
Find sensitive files (backups, configs, source code). Appends filenames to base URL.

.SS Extension Fuzzing
Test multiple file extensions on a base path (e.g., index.php, index.asp, index.html).

.SS Virtual Host Discovery
Enumerate virtual hosts by fuzzing the HTTP Host header.

.SS Subdomain Enumeration
DNS-based subdomain discovery with wildcard detection and multiple resolvers.

.SS Cloud Storage Fuzzing
Discover publicly accessible cloud storage buckets (S3, Azure Blob, GCP, DigitalOcean Spaces).

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Basic directory fuzzing:
.B nemue fuzz https://example.com -b dirs1k

.TP
Recursive directory scan:
.B nemue fuzz https://example.com -b dirs10k -R \-\-max-depth 3

.TP
File discovery with extensions:
.B nemue fuzz https://example.com/index -m ext -e php,asp,html

.TP
Subdomain enumeration:
.B nemue fuzz example.com -m subdomain -b subdomains

.TP
AWS S3 bucket discovery:
.B nemue fuzz company-name -m s3 -b dirs1k

.TP
Filtered fuzzing:
.B nemue fuzz https://example.com -b dirs1k -s 200,301,302 \-\-min-size 1000

.TP
Parameter fuzzing:
.B nemue fuzz "https://api.example.com/users?id=FUZZ" -b params

.TP
WordPress scan with mutations:
.B nemue fuzz https://example.com -b wordpress \-\-mutate

.TP
High-speed fuzzing:
.B nemue fuzz https://example.com -b dirs10k -c 100 -r 200

.TP
Save results to JSON:
.B nemue fuzz https://example.com -b dirs1k -o json -O results.json

.TP
Custom headers and authentication:
.B nemue fuzz https://example.com -b dirs1k -H "Authorization:Bearer token123"

.TP
Vhost discovery:
.B nemue fuzz https://192.168.1.1 -m vhost -b subdomains

.SH PARAMETER FUZZING MODES
.TP
.B sniper
Fuzz one parameter at a time
.TP
.B clusterbomb
Try all combinations of parameters
.TP
.B pitchfork
Synchronized iteration across parameters
.TP
.B replace
Replace all FUZZ keywords simultaneously

.SH OUTPUT FORMATS
.TP
.B text
Human-readable ASCII art output with colors
.TP
.B json
Structured JSON for programmatic processing
.TP
.B csv
Comma-separated values for spreadsheets
.TP
.B markdown
Markdown tables for documentation
.TP
.B html
Interactive HTML report with CSS styling

.SH PERFORMANCE TIPS
.IP \(bu 2
Start with lower concurrency (-c 10-50) to avoid overwhelming servers
.IP \(bu 2
Use rate limiting (-r) to respect server capacity
.IP \(bu 2
Enable wildcard detection to filter false positives
.IP \(bu 2
Use built-in wordlists for faster loading
.IP \(bu 2
Filter by status codes to reduce noise

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Fuzzing completed successfully
.TP
.B 1
Error during fuzzing
.TP
.B 2
Invalid arguments

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nemue (1),
.BR nemue\-scan (1),
.BR gobuster (1),
.BR ffuf (1)

